      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FURY (2) is the one to beat after putting a BM70 away by two and a half lengths at this track as favourite, and his record over this course and distance is a major asset: three wins and two placings from five attempts. The rise to BM76 is the challenge, but he comes into an easier meeting, gets weight relief and reunites with Jarrod Todd, who has won four times on him. BIDEN TIME (6) brings the clearest momentum, having won a BM58 and BM64 at this track at his past two, and 55kg gives him every chance to carry that form up in grade. STORMFRONT (1) has been close in consecutive runs, including second in an Open here when beaten just under a length, and his 1600m record keeps him right in the race despite being a touch costly to follow. TOKYO BANDIT (7) is harder to trust on the raw finishing positions, but he had excuses when slow away and wide last start, and the return of Paul Shiers gives him a path to running better than the form reads.",
